<div class="incident-model-map" role="group" aria-labelledby="incident-model-map-title">
<h3 id="incident-model-map-title">One incident, different records doing different jobs</h3>
<div class="model-intent-row">
<div class="model-node model-intent" data-model-concept="intent"><h4>{{INTENT_ICON}}<span>Intent</span></h4><p>A declared problem or desired change, before its solution is settled.</p><strong>Restore a complete eligible export for {{CASE_ACCOUNT}}</strong></div>
<div class="model-node model-resolution" data-model-concept="intent"><h4>{{INTENT_RESOLUTION_ICON}}<span>Intent Resolution</span></h4><p>The owner’s chosen response and satisfaction test.</p><strong>Choose an export-repair project and the accepted coverage criterion</strong></div>
</div>
<div class="model-lanes">
<div class="model-lane model-product-lane">
<p class="model-lane-label">Value offered over time</p>
<ol class="model-records" role="list">
<li class="model-node" data-model-concept="product"><h4>{{PRODUCT_ICON}}<span>Product</span></h4><p>The durable identity that owns a promise of value.</p><strong>The customer platform</strong></li>
<li class="model-node" data-model-concept="product"><h4>{{PRODUCT_CAPABILITY_ICON}}<span>Product Capability</span></h4><p>The outcome that one product must make possible.</p><strong>Customers can obtain all required export identifiers</strong></li>
<li class="model-node" data-model-concept="product"><h4>{{CAPABILITY_BINDING_ICON}}<span>Capability Realization Binding</span></h4><p>A governed association between exact capability and implementation versions.</p><strong>The selected export-capability revision linked to service revision {{CASE_SERVICE_REVISION}}</strong></li>
<li class="model-node" data-model-concept="work"><h4>{{IMPLEMENTATION_ICON}}<span>Implementation</span></h4><p>The technical realization to build, assess and operate.</p><strong>Service {{CASE_SERVICE_REVISION}} produced {{CASE_OUTPUT}}; revision {{CASE_FIX_REVISION}} is a candidate change</strong></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div class="model-lane model-project-lane">
<p class="model-lane-label">Work organized around the problem</p>
<ol class="model-records" role="list">
<li class="model-node" data-model-concept="project"><h4>{{PROJECT_ICON}}<span>Project</span></h4><p>The durable coordination identity for goals, work, decisions and evidence.</p><strong>The {{CASE_ACCOUNT}} export-repair effort</strong></li>
<li class="model-node" data-model-concept="project"><h4>{{GOAL_ICON}}<span>Goal</span></h4><p>A desired outcome with success conditions and rules for recording achievement.</p><strong>Required identifiers present in an assessed replacement export</strong></li>
<li class="model-node" data-model-concept="work"><h4>{{WORK_ICON}}<span>Work</span></h4><p>A bounded activity with inputs, constraints and an expected result.</p><strong>Investigate the reported omission in {{CASE_OUTPUT}}</strong></li>
<li class="model-node model-agent" data-model-concept="agent"><h4>{{AGENT_ASSIGNMENT_ICON}}<span>Agent Assignment</span></h4><p>The binding that identifies the agent’s participation in this work.</p><strong>Session {{CASE_SESSION}} takes the investigation job, with separate delegation</strong></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div class="model-incident"><h4>Incident · {{CASE_TICKET_ID}}</h4><p>Coordinates response, accountability, communications, recovery and closure for the reported failure. Its response remains open while the repair project and investigation have their own states.</p></div>
<p class="model-map-note">Read the two columns as different responsibilities. The assignment identifies the job; delegation supplies permission, and the agent session brings that job together with its views and temporary working memory.</p>
</div>
